* Simple measurement examples
* transient simulation of two sine signals with different frequencies

vac1   1 0 DC 0  sin(0 1   1.0k 0 0)
vac2   2 0 DC 0  sin(0 1.2 0.9k 0 0)
vout out 0 DC 0  sin(0 1.2 1.3k 0 0)
v0    in 0 DC 0  sin(0 1.2 1.3k 0 100)
R1    in 0 100

.tran  10u 5m 0 10u

** Fails because FROM .. TO sets an interval restriction while WHEN v(1)=-0.4 is (another, but) point one.
** Minor: ngspice-40 does not give the cause of the failure (e.g. LTspice does).
.measure tran exper  FIND v(2) WHEN v(1)=-0.4 FROM=1ms TO=1.1ms

** there is no v(3), but we get a result: yeval2 = 0.9705079 . In LTspice this fails, as it should.
.measure tran yeval2 FIND v(2) WHEN v(1)=v(3) FALL=2

** Here ngspice fails to evaluate '0.9*v(2)' and apparently decides it is either '0.9' or 'v(2)'
.measure tran yeval3 FIND v(2) WHEN v(1)=0.9*v(2)

* This works in LTspice: In ngspice I think only a simple variable can be returned.
* ngspice returns
* yeval4              =  9.000000e-01
.measure tran yeval4 FIND v(1) WHEN v(1)=0.9*v(2)

** This overwrites the previous yeval3 (above) and it would be nice if that was reported.
** In LTspice this is a serious error and the simulator refuses to execute any measurement.
* .measure tran yeval3 FIND v(2) AT=2m
* Changed to yeval5 to see what the result should have been:
.measure tran yeval5 FIND v(2) AT=2m

.end

* ****************************************************************
* LTspice result:
* ****************************************************************
* .measure tran exper find v(2) when v(1)=-0.4 from=1ms to=1.1ms
*  Error: Both a point and interval trigger are specified.

* Measurement "yeval2" FAIL'ed
* yeval3: v(2)=0 at 0
* yeval4: v(1)=0 at 0
* yeval5: v(2)=-1.14088 at 0.002


* ****************************************************************
* NGSPICE vs 40 result:
* ****************************************************************
* Error: measure  exper  find(AT) : out of interval
*  .measure tran exper find v(2) when v(1)=-0.4 from=1ms to=1.1ms failed!

* yeval2              =  9.705079e-01
* yeval3              =  1.014966e+00
* yeval4              =  9.000000e-01
* yeval3              =  -1.140899e+00